The utility to manipulate machine owner keys which are managed in shim.

Policy-controlled MOK management is available without changing the existing
command line:

* `--policy <file>` applies import, delete, revoke, and reset rules from a
  versioned policy file. `MOKUTIL_POLICY` and `/etc/mokutil/policy.conf` are
  discovered when `--policy` is not supplied. If no policy exists, legacy
  behavior is retained.
* `--policy-check <file>` validates a policy without touching EFI variables.
* `--import-list <manifest>` imports a batch from a manifest. Relative paths
  are resolved from the manifest directory, comments are ignored, and
  directories expand to their regular files. The batch is validated in full
  before a MOK request is written.
* Existing `--import`, `--delete`, `--import-hash`, `--delete-hash`,
  `--revoke-import`, and `--revoke-delete` options keep their original syntax.

See `man/mokutil.1` for the policy grammar and examples.

Run the five configuration tests with:

```
make check
```

Covered configurations are legacy/no-policy compatibility, allowed batch
import, deny rules (fingerprint, path, batch size, and CA requirement),
revoke policy, and malformed policy rejection.
